.TH PERLLSP 1 "2026-03-30" "perllsp 0.12.1" "Perl Language Server"
.SH NAME
perllsp \- Perl Language Server Protocol implementation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perllsp
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B perl\-lsp
.B \-\-check
.IR file.pl " [" file2.pm " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B perl\-lsp
is a Language Server Protocol (LSP) server for Perl, providing IDE features
such as diagnostics, completions, go-to-definition, hover, formatting,
code actions, semantic tokens, and more.
It communicates with editors over stdio (default) or TCP socket transport
using the JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol.
.PP
The server uses
.B perl\-parser v3
(a native recursive descent parser) to analyze Perl source code without
requiring a Perl interpreter at runtime.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-stdio
Use stdio for communication.
This is the default transport mode.
.TP
.B \-\-socket
Use TCP socket for communication.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port to listen on when using socket transport.
Default:
.BR 9257 .
Implies
.BR \-\-socket .
.TP
.B \-\-log
Enable logging to stderr.
Logging is also activated when the
.B PERL_LSP_LOG
or
.B RUST_LOG
environment variable is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-feature\-profile " NAME"
Set the feature profile, which controls which LSP capabilities are
advertised to the editor.
Supported values:
.BR auto ", " ga\-lock ", " ga ", " ga_lock ", " prod ", " production ", " all .
.TP
.B \-\-health
Perform a quick health check and print
.RI \(dq ok
.IR "<version>" \(dq
to stdout, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-info
Show server information including version, git tag, feature profile,
number of advertised features, and LSP coverage percentage.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate Perl files and report parse errors in batch mode, then exit.
Requires one or more file arguments.
Exits with status 0 if all files parse successfully, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-features\-json
Output the features catalog as JSON and exit.
The output reflects the active feature profile.
.TP
.BI \-\-completion " SHELL"
Generate shell completion script for the given shell and print it to
stdout, then exit.
Supported shells:
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " powershell .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .perl\-lsp.toml
Project-level configuration file.
When present in the workspace root, the server reads settings from this
file to configure diagnostics, formatting, and other LSP behaviors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PERL_LSP_LOG
When set, enables logging to stderr.
The value is used as a tracing filter directive
(e.g.,
.IR perl_lsp=debug ).
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Alternative environment variable for configuring the tracing filter.
.B PERL_LSP_LOG
takes precedence if both are set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables colored output in
.B \-\-health
and
.B \-\-info
output.
See
.IR https://no\-color.org/ .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the server in stdio mode (default):
.PP
.RS
.nf
perl\-lsp \-\-stdio
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run with the production feature profile:
.PP
.RS
.nf
perl\-lsp \-\-stdio \-\-feature\-profile=prod
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run with logging enabled:
.PP
.RS
.nf
perl\-lsp \-\-stdio \-\-log
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run in socket mode on a specific port:
.PP
.RS
.nf
perl\-lsp \-\-socket \-\-port 9257
.fi
.RE
.PP
Validate Perl files for syntax errors:
.PP
.RS
.nf
perl\-lsp \-\-check lib/MyModule.pm script.pl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install bash completions:
.PP
.RS
.nf
perl\-lsp \-\-completion bash >> ~/.bashrc
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (invalid arguments, parse failures in
.B \-\-check
mode, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR perl (1),
.BR perlcritic (1)
.PP
.UR https://microsoft.github.io/language\-server\-protocol/
Language Server Protocol Specification
.UE
.PP
.UR https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/perl\-lsp
Project Repository
.UE
